n {:value "258910"} "Individual Pursuit (4,000 metres), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "258949"} "Team Pursuit (4,000 metres), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "258920"} "Points Race, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "258948"} "Madison, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "258993"} "Sprint, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "259019"} "Individual Pursuit (4,000 metres), Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "259018"} "Points Race, Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "154983"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "155109"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "308096"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "356781"} "2016"] "\n" [:option {:value "19004957"} "2020"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008756"} "2024"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/219"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Keirin, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "16 August 2008"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/821"} "Laoshan Zixingcheguan, Beijing"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/258931"} "25 from 16 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Twenty-five racers started the keirin, but all eyes were on " [:a {:href "/athletes/90388"} "Chris Hoy"] ", the 2007-08 World Champion, who had already won gold in Beijing in the team sprint. The event was overshadowed by the the failure of three pre-race favorites – former World Champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/106875"} "Teun Mulder"] " of the Netherlands was disqualified in the first-round repêchage; his teammate, " [:a {:href "/athletes/106870"} "Theo Bos"] ", who did not finish the second semi-final, crashing over " [:a {:href "/athletes/113192"} "Kamil Kuczyński"] ", when he fell; and defending Olympic champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/106880"} "Ryan Bayley"] " of Australia, who finished last in the first semi. Hoy made it to the final without being challenged, winning both his rounds. His biggest challengers in the final looked to be Australian " [:a {:href "/athletes/15038"} "Shane Kelly"] " and France’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/90378"} "Arnaud Tournant"] ", but the final was all Hoy, who jumped into the lead shortly after derny exited the track and could not be caught. His teammate, " [:a {:href "/athletes/106883"} "Ross Edgar"] ", outsprinted Japan’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/113174"} "Kiyofumi Nagai"] " for the silver medal, with Kelly placing fourth and Tournant sixth. Keirin is very popular in Japan, where pari-mutuel betting is permitted on the races, but this was the first keirin medal by a Japanese cyclist."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "R1 Rep"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/90388"} "Chris Hoy"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "– (1 h1)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "– (1 h1)"] [:td {} "– (1 h1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/106883"} "Ross Edgar"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "– (1 h3)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "– (1 h2)"] [:td {} "– (2 h1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {